      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to the [[credential-scoping]] article, the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned child process** \u2014 specifically, right before the process starts.\n\nThe key points are:\n\n1. **The Hub doesn\u0027t hold the key**: The Hub process itself never has the API key in its own environment.\n\n2. **Injection happens at spawn time**: A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it only into the spawned Ingest agent child process immediately before that process launches.\n\n3. **Same model for Query agent**: The Query agent receives the credential the same way \u2014 injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from or stored in the Hub\u0027s process environment.\n\nThis design ensures that a compromised or misbehaving Hub cannot leak the credential just by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5258,
      "output_tokens": 217
    }
